{"id":"lines-over-or-under-every-year","title":"Budget lines more than 10% over, or 20% under, in six or more of eight years","question":"Which operating budget lines miss in the same direction year after year?","finding":"18 department lines of the operating funds missed their adopted budget by more than 10% over, or 20% under, in at least six of the eight years and by more than $20 million in all. By chance alone a line of at least $5 million is more than 10% over in 14% of years and more than 20% under in 10%. Most of the largest gaps are bookkeeping (debt service, retirement investment fees and court benefits recorded in a different place from where they were budgeted).","how":"Operating fund category, department and spending character, adopted budget against the ledger, fiscal 2019 to 2026.","limits":"The adopted budget omits supplemental appropriations; enterprise departments and the Retirement System book some costs (debt service, investment fees) to accounts other than the budgeted ones; revenue-backed hospital costs at Public Health are often appropriated during the year.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"department","t":"Department","type":"org"},{"k":"line","t":"Spending character (account code)","type":"text"},{"k":"budget","t":"Adopted, FY2019-26","type":"usd"},{"k":"spent","t":"Spent, FY2019-26","type":"usd"},{"k":"diff","t":"Difference","type":"usd"},{"k":"yearsOver","t":"Years >10% over","type":"int"},{"k":"yearsUnder","t":"Years >20% under","type":"int"}],"rows":[{"department":"PUC Public Utilities Commsn","line":"DEBT_SERVICE","budget":3452562674,"spent":7926620,"diff":-3444636054,"yearsOver":0,"yearsUnder":8},{"department":"DPH Public Health","line":"NON_PERS_SVCS","budget":5910622113,"spent":7107633386,"diff":1197011273,"yearsOver":7,"yearsUnder":0},{"department":"DPH Public Health","line":"MTL_SUPP","budget":1331008947,"spent":1622074505,"diff":291065558,"yearsOver":7,"yearsUnder":0},{"department":"RET Retirement System","line":"NON_PERS_SVCS",